antics":{"integerEncoding":"BigInt with checked fixed-width arithmetic; usize/isize assume 64 bits","assumptions":["Rust integer arithmetic uses checked overflow behavior (debug/test profile); release wrapping arithmetic is outside this draft contract","String case conversion depends on the source and host Unicode tables","Concrete admitted constants require bounded checked evaluation with original parser source links; const fn runtime eligibility alone proves no all-input compile-time behavior","Immutable strings encode scalar values; monomorphic tagged values encode Option/Result; vectors/slices are immutable arrays"],"observation":"checked value results, local scalar mutation, immutable constructors, lazy future polling and named host effects; carried items supply no executable behavior"},"counts":{"executable":1,"executableFunctions":0,"executableConstants":1,"executableTypes":0,"executableConstructors":0,"carried":7,"preserved":9},"items":[{"term":"trivia","name":null,"span":{"start":0,"end":1245,"unit":"utf16","byteStart":0,"byteEnd":1251},"sha256":"d89b8b87c5a08ab436a17fffb0712a16690f1f87c399b5022f8038af06943f08","source":"//! Response hardening for the admin listener.\n//!\n//! The admin console keeps its credential in `localStorage` (see `ui/src/api.js`),\n//! which makes two browser-side attacks worth closing at the HTTP layer rather\n//! than trusting the bundle:\n//!\n//! * **script injection** — any script that runs on this origin can read the\n//!   token. React escapes what it renders, but a Content-Security-Policy that\n//!   allows scripts only from this origin means an injected `<script src=…>` or\n//!   an exfiltrating `fetch()` to another host fails even if escaping ever does;\n//! * **clickjacking** — the console has one-click destructive actions (revoke,\n//!   rotate). `frame-ancestors 'none'` plus `X-Frame-Options: DENY` keeps it out\n//!   of a third-party frame, and `form-action 'none'` keeps a submitted form\n//!   from posting the page's data elsewhere.\n//!\n//! `style-src` has to allow inline styles: Chakra/emotion injects its rules into\n//! a `<style>` element at runtime. That is the one relaxation, and it does not\n//! help an attacker reach the token.\n//!\n//! These are defence in depth. The primary control is still that the admin\n//! listener does not exist unless the operator gives it a port, and binds to\n//! loopback when they do.\n\n","status":"preserved","diagnostic":null,"comment":true},{"term":"use","name":"axum","span":{"start":1245,"end":1272,"unit":"utf16","byteStart":1251,"byteEnd":1278},"sha256":"e098e0cc91595e54509add946d245738413ef8be724d5ee3acf5fc2d1fcb7917","source":"use axum::extract::Request;","status":"carried","diagnostic":{"kind":"unsupported","message":"draft item use: no supported library declaration emission","span":{"start":1245,"end":1272},"details":{}},"comment":false,"configuration":{"status":"active","attributes":[],"diagnostics":[]}},{"term":"trivia","name":null,"span":{"start":1272,"end":1273,"unit":"utf16","byteStart":1278,"byteEnd":1279},"sha256":"01ba4719c80b6fe911b091a7c05124b64eeece964e09c058ef8f9805daca546b","source":"\n","status":"preserved","diagnostic":null},{"term":"use","name":"axum","span":{"start":1273,"end":1311,"unit":"utf16","byteStart":1279,"byteEnd":1317},"sha256":"307f457e1b4782fae8d1353ee439cb25c1db267d6a00e1a2f5db8feca8d0d95c","source":"use axum::http::{HeaderValue, header};","status":"carried","diagnostic":{"kind":"unsupported","message":"draft item use: no supported library declaration emission","span":{"start":1273,"end":1311},"details":{}},"comment":false,"configuration":{"status":"active","attributes":[],"diagnostics":[]}},{"term":"trivia","name":null,"span":{"start":1311,"end":1312,"unit":"utf16","byteStart":1317,"byteEnd":1318},"sha256":"01ba4719c80b6fe911b091a7c05124b64eeece964e09c058ef8f9805daca546b","source":"\n","status":"preserved","diagnostic":null},{"term":"use","name":"axum","span":{"start":1312,"end":1339,"unit":"utf16","by